         "step": 1,
         "text": "A degree 3 polynomial needs the values through order 3: \\( h(3) = 2 \\), \\( h'(3) = 0 \\), \\( h''(3) = -4 \\), \\( h'''(3) = 6 \\). The value of order 4 is not used.",
         "mathjson": 6
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Divide each by the matching factorial: \\( \\frac{2}{0!} = 2 \\), \\( \\frac{0}{1!} = 0 \\), \\( \\frac{-4}{2!} = -2 \\), \\( \\frac{6}{3!} = 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": 1
